# r2 bidirectionality verification — bundled default catalog (ticket #9)

Per the R2 rule: for one representative test per behavior family, verify the
test genuinely gates the behavior — PASS on the real code, break the code,
confirm a REAL vitest FAIL, restore, PASS again. Three families were probed:
the loadCatalog source default (data layer), the init bundled branch (store),
and the banner string (UI).

Baseline: `npm test` → Test Files 11 passed (11), Tests 222 passed (222).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Family 1 — loadCatalog legacy-row default (src/data/catalog-store.ts)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Break: `source: stored.source ?? { kind: "user" }`
    →  `source: stored.source as CatalogSource`   (drop the legacy default)

`npx vitest run src/data/catalog-store.test.ts`:

    × revives a legacy row (no source field) as user 4ms
    FAIL  src/data/catalog-store.test.ts > catalog cache — source provenance
          (ticket #9) > revives a legacy row (no source field) as user
    AssertionError: expected undefined to deeply equal { kind: 'user' }
    Tests  1 failed | 6 passed (7)

Restore → the `?? { kind: "user" }` default → PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Family 2 — init bundled fallback branch (src/state/store.ts)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Break: `bundled = await bundledDocsProvider();`
    →  `bundled = null; // bundled fallback disabled`   (never consult provider)

`npx vitest run src/state/store.test.ts`:

    × empty cache + bundled provider → bundled-ready, cached, source persisted
    × version-stale cache + bundled provider → bundled-ready
    × bundled-ready but save fails (broken IDB) → usable this session + note
    × uploading over a bundled catalog flips the source to user
    FAIL  … > empty cache + bundled provider → bundled-ready …
    AssertionError: expected 'needs-upload' to be 'ready' // Object.is equality
    FAIL  … > uploading over a bundled catalog flips the source to user
    AssertionError: expected null to match object { kind: 'bundled' }
    Tests  4 failed | 28 passed (32)

Restore → `await bundledDocsProvider()` → PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Family 3 — provenance banner string (src/ui/App.tsx BundledBanner)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Break: banner copy `bundled game data · …`
    →  `BROKEN game data · …`

`npx vitest run src/ui/smoke.test.tsx`:

    × renders the banner with the exact provenance string when source is bundled
    FAIL  src/ui/smoke.test.tsx > App provenance banner (ticket #9) >
          renders the banner with the exact provenance string when source is
          bundled
    AssertionError: expected '<p class="bundled-banner">BROKEN game…' to contain
      'bundled game data · Steam build 23855724 (2026-04-30) — upload your own
       Docs.json if your game is newer'
    Tests  1 failed | 15 passed (16)

Restore → `bundled game data · …` → PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Family 4 — unavailable classification / data preservation (boundary r1 fold)
  (src/data/catalog-store.ts loadCatalog access-failure catch)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Break: `catch { return { status: "unavailable" }; }`
    →  `catch { return { status: "stale" }; }`   (re-conflate access failure
                                                   with stale → destructive save)

`npx vitest run src/data/catalog-store.test.ts src/state/store.test.ts`:

    × returns unavailable (not stale) on an IDB access failure (boundary r1 fold)
    × IDB unavailable (broken open) → bundled-ready WITHOUT save + distinct note
    × preserves an unreadable user row — no destructive bundled overwrite
    FAIL  src/data/catalog-store.test.ts > … > returns unavailable (not stale)
          on an IDB access failure
    AssertionError: expected 'stale' to be 'unavailable' // Object.is equality
    FAIL  src/state/store.test.ts > … > IDB unavailable (broken open) →
          bundled-ready WITHOUT save + distinct note
    AssertionError: expected 'bundled catalog loaded but could not …' to be
      'cached data couldn't be read this session — using bundled data'
    FAIL  src/state/store.test.ts > … > preserves an unreadable user row — no
          destructive bundled overwrite (data-loss proof)
    AssertionError: expected 'bundled catalog loaded but could not …' to be
      'cached data couldn't be read this session — using bundled data'
    Tests  3 failed | 39 passed (42)

The data-loss proof failing on the reverted classification is the key signal:
with the access failure re-mapped to stale, init takes the SAVE path and the
memoized-healthy connection lets the put overwrite the user row — exactly the
defect. Restore → `unavailable` → PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Final: `npm test` → Test Files 11 passed (11), Tests 225 passed (225).

All four families are bidirectional: the tests fail when their behavior is
removed and pass when it is restored — they gate real behavior, not tautology.
